==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Li'l Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*2 [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>.
*1 [[Formicidaean Ariant]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*1 [[Mini Angel Cyclone]] spawns once 100 Cat Units have been defeated.
*1 [[Mini Angel Cyclone]] spawns once 200 Cat Units have been defeated.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] spawns as the boss.
**4 [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**4 [[Formicidaean Ariant]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**4 [[Mini Angel Cyclone]]s spawn, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage has a lot of Mini Angel Cyclones, so make sure to bring [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] because they can push hard and make it difficult to reach THE FOLIVOREAN. The best option for the Formicidaean Ariants is to use [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]]. As for the Imperator Saels, a combination of [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] to Freeze and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] to chip them down works well. THE FOLIVOREAN can be taken care of with [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N006 (Special Cat)|Fallen Bear Cat]] if the player has them.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Talents|Ultra Talented]] [[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)]]: With Strong Against Aku and Zombie, along with Surge Immunity, Hayabusa can do large amounts of damage to Formicidaean Ariant and THE FOLIVOREAN. Just be careful of the Mini Angel Cyclones, as they can push in very easily, so use Ramen Cat to prevent this.
*[[Dioramos (Uber Rare Cat)|Ascendant Dioramos]]: His main role here is pushing back and Slowing the Mini Angel Cyclones. In addition, he was great bulk and DPS, so he'll be able to do massive amounts of damage while also not being juggled.

==Trivia==
*Like [[Crag of Monte Cristo]], Beast of Monte Cristo is a reference to the novel [[wikipedia:The Count of Monte Cristo|''The Count of Monte Cristo'']]. Its Japanese name, Jyuukustuou (獣窟王, "Beast Cave King"), is based on ''Gankustuou'' (巌窟王, "Cavern King"), the Japanese title of the novel and its [[wikipedia:Gankutsuou: The Count of Monte Cristo|anime adaptation]]. Within this context, [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] may represent the [[wikia:gankutsuou:The Count of Monte Cristo (character)|titular count]] of the anime, who turned blue after being demonically possessed by [[wikia:gankutsuou:The King of the Cavern|The King of the Cavern]].

